// List the drawing sizes you have configured in the drawing layout
// definitions and the paper size name the drawing is designed for.
// Dimensions are in mm with a ‘.’ for the decimal place regardless of
// the operating system’s regional settings and a ‘,’ to separate each
// field.
//
// Format is <PaperSizeName>, <DrawingLandscapeWidth>, <DrawingLandscapeHeight>, <DrawingLeftMargin>, <DrawingBottomMargin>, <DrawingRightMargin>, <DrawingTopMargin>
//
// <PaperSizeName> = Name of the paper size in the paper sizes
//  file. Multiple entries are allowed in this file for the same paper
//  size name.
//
//    +-----------------------------+
//    |Paper                        |
//    |  +-----------------------+  |
//    |  |Drawing                |  |
//    |  |  +-----------------+  |  |
//    |  |  | Area            |  |  |
//    |  |  | of interest     |  |  |
//    |  |  | (Drawing frame) |  |  |
//    |  |  |                 |  |  |
//    |  |  |                 |  |  |
//    |  |  |                 |  |  |
//    |  |  |                 |  |  |
//    |  |  |                 |  |  |
//    |  |  |                 |  |  |
//    |  |  |                 |  |  |
//    |  |  +-----------------+  |  |
//    |  |                       |  |
//    |  +-----------------------+  |
//    |                             |
//    +-----------------------------+
//
// <DrawingLandscapeWidth>, <DrawingLandscapeHeight> = These should
//  match a specific drawing layout width and height (either a fix size
//  width and height or a calculated size width and height).
//
// <DrawingLeftMargin>, <DrawingBottomMargin>, <DrawingRightMargin>,
//  <DrawingTopMargin> = These are optional. If not specified the
//  default values are used.
//
//   - The area of the drawing that is of interest and that needs to
//     be included in a print is the area specified by
//     <DrawingLandscapeWidth>, <DrawingLandscapeHeight> less any
//     margins specified.
//
//   - The area of interest is usually the outer boundary of the
//     drawing frame (so that the frame itself is printed).
//
//   - If <DrawingBottomMargin> is not specified then it is set to
//     <DrawingLeftMargin>
//
//   - If <DrawingRightMargin> is not specified then it is set to
//     <DrawingLeftMargin>
//
//   - If <DrawingTopMargin> is not specified then it is set to
//     <DrawingBottomMargin>
//
//   - Default margins are specified using the paper size name
//     <DEFAULT> and setting <DrawingLandscapeWidth> and
//     <DrawingLandscapeHeight> to 0.
//
//
// e.g.:
//      A4, 287, 210, 5
//     11X17, 406, 254, 15.8, 12.7, 10, 12.7
//
// In addition to the internal margins explicitly specified in each
// entry, an external margin is implied by the difference between the
// size of the drawing and the size of the paper. External margins
// will automatically be determined to place the drawing centrally on
// the paper where an entry is matched.
//
// When no entry matches a drawing size, there is no paper size to
// infer the external margin from, so the values from the
// <PAPERDEFAULT> entry are used.
//
// e.g.:
//      <DEFAULT>           0,  0,  5
//      <PAPERDEFAULT>      0,  0,  5
//
// Defines default overall margins of 10mm around each side of the
// area of interest.
//
// File must be saved as a Unicode text format file
//
<DEFAULT>,          0,      0,      5
<PAPERDEFAULT>,     0,      0,      5
4*A3, 841, 594, 0, 0, 0, 0